From f0c2bb973c2c8fafcb10ae15199d74828808999b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vauzi-17 <189964753+Vauzi-17@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:20:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/21] android: Rebase the ntdll loader patches onto the
 GE-Proton hotfixes.

GE-Proton11-7's ntdll-remove-redundant-packed-split-lock and
ntdll-prefer-native-version-resource-heuristics change the lines next to
two hunks of the Android patches, so git apply refused
arm64ec/ and x86_64/dlls_ntdll_unix_loader_c.patch and
common/dlls_ntdll_unix_unix_private_h.patch. They are regenerated with a
three-way merge; the lines they add and remove are unchanged.

The build scripts ignored a failed git apply and built on without the
patch. A patch that does not apply now stops the build.
---
 android/patches/arm64ec/dlls_ntdll_unix_loader_c.patch | 10 +++++-----
 .../common/dlls_ntdll_unix_unix_private_h.patch        | 10 +++++-----
 android/patches/x86_64/dlls_ntdll_unix_loader_c.patch  | 10 +++++-----
 build-scripts/build-step-arm64ec.sh                    |  5 ++---
 build-scripts/build-step-x86_64.sh                     |  5 ++---
 5 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

